        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        {
          "category": "general",
          "text": "DOMPurify 3.1.3 through 3.3.1 and 2.5.3 through 2.5.8, fixed in commit 2726c74, contain a cross-site scripting vulnerability that allows attackers to bypass attribute sanitization by exploiting five missing rawtext elements (noscript, xmp, noembed, noframes, iframe) in the SAFE_FOR_XML regex. Attackers can include payloads like \u003c/noscript\u003e\u003cimg src=x onerror=alert(1)\u003e in attribute values to execute JavaScript when sanitized output is placed inside these unprotected rawtext contexts.",
          "title": "CVE description"
        }
      ],
